     The way energy is used worldwide is not sustainable. It is well-documented
that the use of these fuels is depleting the world’s natural resource reserves, harming
communities in terms of health and displacement, and polluting the air and water
in local environments. The drilling, refining, and transporting of oil leads to spills
on land and in oceans, and when petrol-based fuels are used to power machines and
automobiles, the air is polluted with greenhouse gases and particulate matter such
as carbon dioxide, carbon monoxide, sulfur, and nitrous oxide emissions.
